hypotheses.statement:
The aim is that, for every interval $I\subseteq Y\subseteq E_0$ with infinite gap, some basis $B$ satisfies the following alternative [(eq:interval-alternative)](#eq:interval-alternative): $$\label{eq:interval-alternative}
 B\subseteq I,\qquad I\subseteq B\subseteq Y,
 \qquad\text{or}\qquad Y\subseteq B.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
There is an ultrafilter $\mathcal U$ on $D$ disjoint from $\mathcal K$, containing every $G_t$, and satisfying $$\label{eq:finitely-many-columns}
 X\in\mathcal U\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \{t<\mathfrak c:X\subseteq_{\mathcal K}G_t\}
 \text{ is finite}.$$

Let $\mathcal T$ be a family of fewer than $\mathfrak c$ admissible subsets of $E_0$. Suppose $A\subseteq Z\subseteq E_0$, that $A$ is not Upper and $Z$ is not Lower, and that, for every $T\in\mathcal T$, $$\label{eq:available-separation}
 T\setminus A\notin\mathcal J_0,
 \qquad Z\setminus T\notin\mathcal J_0.$$ Then there is an admissible $B$ between $A$ and $Z$ such that $B\setminus T$ and $T\setminus B$ are $\mathcal J_0$-positive for every $T\in\mathcal T$.

evidence.quote:
For a nontrivial increasing property of $r$-uniform hypergraphs on $n\ge r$ vertices, where $r\ge3$, and every $0<\varepsilon<1/2$, $$p_{1-\varepsilon}-p_\varepsilon
 \le\frac{2C_r}{(\log n)^{r/(r-1)}}
                  \log\frac{1-\varepsilon}{\varepsilon}.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
Let $r+1\le m\le n$ be integers and set $k=\sigma\log m/64$. For $B$ chosen uniformly among the $m$-subsets of $[n]$, $$\label{eq:block}
 \sum_{S\subseteq E}
 \Pr_B(1\le|S\cap F_B|\le k)\widehat f(S)^2
 \le m^{-1/4}\frac{rm}{n}I_p(f).$$

Let $n\ge r\ge3$ and $1\le m\le n$ be integers, let $k>0$, and put $$\alpha=\frac r{r-1},\qquad L=(k/r)^\alpha.$$ Suppose $$\label{eq:capture-condition}
 rL\frac{m-1}{n-1}\le\frac12.$$ For a uniform $m$-subset $B$ of $[n]$ and every $S\subseteq E_{n,r}$ with $1\le|S|\le L$, $$\label{eq:capture}
 \Pr_B(1\le|S\cap F_B|\le k)\ge\frac{m}{2n}.$$

For a nontrivial increasing property of $r$-uniform hypergraphs on $n\ge r$ vertices, where $r\ge3$, and every $0<\varepsilon<1/2$, $$p_{1-\varepsilon}-p_\varepsilon
 \le\frac{2C_r}{(\log n)^{r/(r-1)}}
                  \log\frac{1-\varepsilon}{\varepsilon}.$$
